@startuml
' Sequence diagram: checkout confirmation flow with async pickup email dispatch
' Shows the full timeline from client request through email delivery

actor "Client" as C
participant "Checkout Controller" as Ctrl
participant "checkoutmodel" as CM
participant "clientmodel" as CLM
participant "mail.Mailer" as Mail
participant "SMTP Server" as SMTP
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Checkout Confirmation (synchronous) ==

C -> Ctrl: POST /checkouts/confirm\n(session_id, items, client_email, value_paid)
activate Ctrl

Ctrl -> CM: Confirm(ctx, pool, sessionID, req)
activate CM

CM -> DB: BEGIN transaction
CM -> DB: check idempotency (session + ref)
CM -> DB: resolve cart + validate stock
CM -> DB: write checkout + reserve packages
CM -> DB: COMMIT
CM --> Ctrl: ConfirmResponse{UniqueID, QrCode, Status}
deactivate CM

Ctrl --> C: 200 OK {unique_id, qr_code, status}
deactivate Ctrl

== Post-Checkout Email (async, best-effort) ==

Ctrl -> Ctrl: createClientAfterCheckout\n(after response sent)
activate Ctrl

Ctrl -> Ctrl: derive client name from email
Ctrl -> Ctrl: generate + hash password

Ctrl -> CLM: CreateAndAssociate(ctx, pool, name, email, hash, cartID)
activate CLM

CLM -> DB: BEGIN transaction
CLM -> DB: find user by email

alt email not found (new user)
  CLM -> DB: create user + client record
  CLM --> Ctrl: (clientID, isNew=true)
else email found (existing)
  CLM -> DB: verify existing client
  CLM --> Ctrl: (clientID, isNew=false)
end

CLM -> DB: update cart client_id
CLM -> DB: COMMIT
deactivate CLM

Ctrl -> CM: ResolvePickupEmailData(ctx, db, items)
activate CM
CM -> DB: query packages JOIN products\nJOIN consignments JOIN pickup_locations
CM --> Ctrl: []PickupGroup (grouped by pickup location)
deactivate CM

Ctrl -> Ctrl: build PickupEmailData{OrderID, QrCode, Groups, IsNewUser, ...}

Ctrl -> Mail: SendPickupConfirmation(ctx, to, data)
activate Mail

Mail -> Mail: render order info section\n(order ID, QR code, items by pickup)
note right of Mail: ALWAYS included

alt IsNewUser == true
  Mail -> Mail: ALSO render login section\n(name, password, login/reset URLs)
  note right of Mail: additional block — new users only
else IsNewUser == false
  note right of Mail: skip login section (existing users)
end

Mail -> SMTP: send email (subject + HTML body)
activate SMTP
SMTP --> Mail: accepted
deactivate SMTP

Mail --> Ctrl: nil (or error logged)
deactivate Mail

deactivate Ctrl

note over Ctrl, Mail
  Email sending is best-effort: failures are logged
  but never fail the checkout response
end note

@enduml
